Questions have been raised about sharing a nethack playground:
[] Just how much would the overhead be to store saved games/bones/etc
[] in plain ASCII or whatever to give this compatability ??

The ascii files such as help files can, of course, be shared now.
The bones and save files, if converted to ASCII, would increase too
much in size.  The proper way to do it is to adopt a standard binary
machine independent format such as XDR (Sun's non-proprietary external
data representation) which is available on many different platforms.

It would probably be best to include a build option to optionally use
xdr.  We could then allow people to grab and implement an xdr library
on their own on all platforms of interest and then build and install
nethack.  Sites without this interest could proceed, as now, in a
machine-specific way.

